{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791277204,"nonce":"I9kRFrBjZN0Msdpeeor8qDrmIes=","title":"Run on Ash's card-marking GC: every HDLL declares the write barrier","message":"Ash 88c0c7b (ash git-bug 797b910) adds ASH_GC_CARDS=1: a minor collection scans the 512-byte cards written since the last one instead of whole written 32 KB blocks. It turns on only when every loaded HDLL exports ash_hdll_barrier_aware, which promises the library never stores a GC pointer into a GC object except through an hl_* runtime function.\n\n**Status (2026-10-06)**\n- blinc_abi: audited and exports it. It holds Haxe objects only through hl_add_root slots in native memory (hl::Rooted), and writes numbers and bytes into GC buffers.\n- hlwgpu (xgpu.hdll): asked hlwgpu-f8 to audit and export.\n- hlwindow (xwindow.hdll): asked xwindow-fa to audit and export.\n\n**Then**\n- run the suites and the Studio3D flight with ASH_GC_CARDS=1 ASH_GC_CARD_VERIFY=abort, to catch any store the barrier misses;\n- measure the flight's minor pauses with ASH_GC_CARDS=1 against page protection (last: minors 12.8-19 ms, one full at 57 ms) and send the numbers to ash-75, who wants them before making card mode the default.","files":null}]}